">Hejaz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> as the Kingdom of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, now the Saudi National Day.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1938</span><span class="rf-text">Vast oil reserves are discovered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">Al-Ahsa</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>; full-scale development begins in 1941 under the American-controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saudi-aramco">Aramco</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1973</span><span class="rf-text">Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> leads an oil embargo against the Western countries that supported Israel in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yom-kippur-war">Yom Kippur War</a>, and oil prices quadruple.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1979</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-revolution">Iranian Revolution</a> and the seizure of the Grand Mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> by Islamist militants, retaken after ten days, push the royal family towards stricter religious observance and a greater role for the ulema.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1990</span><span class="rf-text">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> invades Kuwait, King Fahd asks the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to intervene and allows American and coalition troops to be stationed in the kingdom; Saudi forces join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-war">Gulf War</a> of 1991.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1992</span><span class="rf-text">King Fahd introduces the Basic Law in March; the Consultative Council of sixty appointed members is inaugurated in December 1993.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2015</span><span class="rf-text">Saudi <a class="enc-link" href=